        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Community Gives Back: Record-Breaking $3.88 Million Raised through the 18th Tin Cup Challenge!</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/63742.webp" alt="Community Gives Back: Record-Breaking $3.88 Million Raised through the 18th Tin Cup Challenge!" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p>The Community Foundation of Teton Valley proudly announced record-breaking results at the 18<sup>th</sup>&nbsp;Tin Cup Challenge Awards Ceremony on Wednesday evening. This annual event brings together nonprofit leaders, donors, and volunteers to celebrate the power of generosity in Teton Valley.</p>

<p><em>“This year, we had our most successful Tin Cup Challenge yet, raising an astounding&nbsp;<strong>$3,881,656 – a 15% increase&nbsp;</strong>over last year,”</em>&nbsp;said Bonnie Self, Executive Director of the Community Foundation of Teton Valley.&nbsp;<em>“These results demonstrate the extraordinary value of local nonprofits and the unwavering generosity of our community.”</em></p>

<h3><strong>Unprecedented Community Impact</strong></h3>

<ul>
<li><strong>Total Raised:</strong>&nbsp;$3,881,656&nbsp;<em>(15% increase over 2024)</em></li>

<li><strong>Challenger Fund:</strong>&nbsp;$1,239,782&nbsp;<em>(4% increase over 2024)</em></li>

<li><strong>Designated Gifts to Nonprofits:</strong>&nbsp;$2,641,874&nbsp;<em>(21% increase over 2024)</em></li>

<li><strong>Donors:</strong>&nbsp;1,623 individuals&nbsp;<em>(20% increase over 2024)</em>&nbsp;– one in three Teton Valley households!</li>

<li><strong>Cumulative Impact</strong><strong>:</strong>&nbsp;More than&nbsp;<strong>$30.8 million</strong>&nbsp;raised in 18 years for a community of 12,000+ residents</li>
</ul>

<p>These funds will directly fuel programs that provide health and human services, education, recreation, arts and culture, conservation, and more. In addition to designated funds, this year’s awards included a&nbsp;<strong>52% Match Grant</strong><strong>&nbsp;on the first $25,000</strong>&nbsp;raised by each participating nonprofit during the Giving Period.</p>

<p>The 2025 Tin Cup Challenge was made possible through the support of&nbsp;<strong>228 Business &amp; Community Challengers, 69 Friends of the Challenge, 6,996 designated contributions, 64 participating nonprofits, and 672 volunteer hours.</strong>&nbsp;The evening’s Awards Celebration was filled with gratitude, joy, and inspiration as neighbors came together to celebrate shared impact.&nbsp;</p>

<p>Without nonprofits and dedicated donors, the landscape of Teton Valley would be vastly different. Our community&#8217;s health relies on the success and vitality of local nonprofits. Thanks to the Community Foundation of Jackson Hole for their partnership and to all who made the 18th Annual Tin Cup Challenge our most successful event yet. Tin Cup illustrates the remarkable impact of generosity and collaboration.&nbsp;Join us in continuing this legacy at&nbsp;www.cftetonvalley.org.</p>

